{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1793309333,"nonce":"uR8RYjqW20XgEaBc+yChb0yuWjw=","message":"Fixed in 9484e80dc2fd59be63b861e3bef37476dd2d34a4 (local, unpushed).\n\nNegative on 34745978: the dedicated API left a red 50%-opacity dynamic root blue at (25,105), [0,0,255,255] instead of [128,0,128,255]. Log /private/tmp/blinc-overlay-tree-negative.log. The old entry drained only the static batch and used separate primitive/text/image dispatch.\n\nThe dedicated entry now calls the shared ordered frame pipeline in load mode. Static/dynamic groups, collected text/styled text/SVG/images, canvases, paths, external callbacks/mesh output and native animation bakes retain normal composition. A private FrameCache moves main CPU replay and promoted textures aside during the fresh paint, then restores them. Temporary overlay bakes return to the existing pool; the dedicated entry retains no replay batch. Glass has one independent reusable half-resolution backdrop. Main viewport and backdrop are restored. Global RenderState cursor/selection overlays are not replayed by this tree-only API. Same-tree paints invalidate replaced main paint records; atlas growth/reclamation invalidates saved glyph replay. Normal reclamation remains enabled.\n\n11 new controls cover the negative; existing and transparent destinations/repeated loads; static/dynamic and foreground/background owners; unified/legacy text, samples1/4 and DPI1/2; live binding/CSS endpoints and clip frames; fresh CSS promotion and same-tree invalidation; entry state without duplicated global cursors; paths/raw images/stacks; grouped and independent callback/mesh output and display scale; single callback execution with glass and alpha-bearing image dispatch; independent main cache/texture/backdrop ownership; and atlas pressure/reclamation with main replay recovery. Corrected early fixture mistakes included a delimiter, sampling a foreground canvas as